%description:

TcpSpoof.srcAddress:invalid -- an address that the node does not have stops the run with an error.

The claim (TcpSpoof.ned): "Sends fabricated TCP packets. ... Compatible with both IPv4
(~Ipv4) and IPv6 (~Ipv6)." TcpSpoof::sendSpoofPacket() sends one segment at the time t: a
header of 20 bytes without options and data, with the window 16384, no ACK, and the SYN bit
of isSYN.

The claim (TcpSpoof.ned): "Local address; may be left empty ("")".

The classes: empty ("", the default: the network layer writes the address of the outgoing
interface), local (an address of the node: the segment carries it, also when the segment
leaves on another interface), and invalid (an address that the node does not have). The code:
TcpSpoof::sendSpoofPacket() resolves the value and puts it into the L3AddressReq of the
segment; Ipv4::encapsulate() takes an address that is not unspecified, and stops the run when
no interface of the node has it, because TcpSpoof does not set nonLocalSrcAddress. This test separates "invalid" from the other classes.

Node under test: the router; The network is TapRouterNetwork: host1 -- tap -- router -- host2. The router has TcpSpoof
in place of its TCP (precondition). The spoof sends one SYN at 1 s from the port 5000 to
host1:1000; the segment leaves the router on eth0, the interface to host1. The tap drops the segment after the router sends
it: the TCP of a receiver cannot take a segment of TcpSpoof (finding PF-11). Observation: level 0, the run stops at 1 s with the error of
Ipv4::encapsulate().

%# parameter: TcpSpoof.srcAddress
%# class: invalid
%# value: "10.99.0.1"
%# key: *.router.tcp.srcAddress
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpSpoofSrcAddressInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.router.tcp.srcAddress = "10.99.0.1"    # the parameter under test
*.host1.numApps = 0
*.router.hasTcp = true
*.router.tcp.typename = "TcpSpoof"
*.router.tcp.destAddress = "host1"
*.router.tcp.srcPort = 5000
*.router.tcp.destPort = 1000
*.router.tcp.seqNo = 12345
*.router.tcp.t = 1s
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
Wrong source address 10\.99\.0\.1 in \(inet::Packet\)spoof: no interface with such address
